  "layout_note": "PSALM-BOUNDARY page (OT2 1610): the tail of Psalm 115 (Vulgate; vv.2-10 — v1 is on p210) followed by the COMPLETE Psalm 116 (Vulgate = the 2-verse 'Laudate Dominum omnes gentes'), with its 'PSALME CXVI.' heading, italic Argument, drop-cap 'P', and vv.1-2. Body scripture is roman (real w: 'What', 'wil'); the lettered interleaved annotations (d-p for Ps115; a-d for Ps116) and the italic Argument are the vv-face (confirmed: 'Alvvayes' note m, 'vvhom'/'Ievves' Ps116 notes). '†' verse markers throughout; verse numbers at left of body; two right-margin gloss-annotations (o, p) + a right-margin key ('the 6. key'); left-margin cross-ref 'Rom. 15. v. 11.'. Foot: signature 'Cc 2' + catchword 'PSALME'. Excluded: hand-inked 'II' top-left, red papal-keys shield, www.fatimamovement.com watermark.",
