  "apparatus": [
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "d", "anchor_verse": "115:2", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "In the middes of my great affliction I profeſſed, that al mans helpe is vaine, falſe, deceipful, and defectiue, and therfore our truſt muſt be in God only." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "e,f", "anchor_verse": "115:3", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "Conſidering that God hath not only geuen, and beſtovved manie great benefites vpon me, and al mankind, but alſo hath rendered good for euil, mercie for our ſinnes, vve hauing rendered euil for good: vvhat novv ſhal I render, ſayth a true penitent, for al that he hath thus rendered to me, deſeruing ſo euil?" },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "g,h", "anchor_verse": "115:4", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "Seing I am not able to render anie thing vvorthie of Gods fauoure to me, yet I vvil do that I can: I vvil gratfully accept his great benefite. the cuppe of Chriſts paſſion, vvhich he druunke for mankind, h and vvil praiſe, and cal vpon his name." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "i,k,l", "anchor_verse": "115:5", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "I vvil pay voluntarie vovves, k for Gods glorie, and edification of others. l yea I vvil offer my life, and ſuffer death, vvhen Gods glorie ſhal require it, in vvhoſe ſight, the death of Sainctes is precious, and moſt highly eſteemed." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "m,n", "anchor_verse": "115:7", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "Alvvayes vnderſtood, that ſuch as ſuffer perſecution, be in good ſtate of their ſoules, the true ſeruantes of God, n the children of the Church his handmaide." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "o", "anchor_verse": "115:8", "position": "right_margin", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "Deliuered me from captiuitie of ſinne." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "p", "anchor_verse": "115:10", "position": "right_margin", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "In the Church of the faithful." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "a,b", "anchor_verse": "116:1", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "Not only ſome, but al nations of the Gentiles: b and al Ievves, (Chriſts Redemption being abundantly ſufficient for al) are inuited to praiſe God." },
    { "role": "annotation", "ref_letter": "c,d", "anchor_verse": "116:2", "typeface": "italic-vv", "text": "Becauſe he hath multiplied his mercie to vs Gentiles, to vvhom he made no promiſe: d and moſt truly performed his promiſe made to the Ievves," }
  ],
